hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17136","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruasi narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi, from Humayd al-Himyari, he said: I met a man of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who accompanied him like Abu Hurayrah accompanied him, and he added nothing for me over three words. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man does not wash from the remainder of a woman, nor does she wash from his remainder, nor does he urinate in his bathing place, nor does he comb every day."
"17137","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, he said: I met a man who had accompanied the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, four years as Abu Hurayrah accompanied him four years. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us that one of us comb every day, and that he urinate in his bathing place, and that a woman wash with the remainder of a man, and that a man wash with the remainder of a woman, but let them scoop together."
"17138","Muhammad, he is Ibn Jafar, narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Ishaq, he is Ibn Suwayd, from Abu Habibah, from that man, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a need, and he saw khaluq upon me. He said: Go and wash it. So I washed it. Then I returned to him. He said: Go and wash it. So I went and fell into a well, and I took a tuft and began following it. Then I returned to him. He said: Your need."
"24083","Narrated to us Ismail, narrated to us Ibn Awn, from Mujahid, he said: Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah was commander over us in the sea for six years. So he addressed us one day and said: We entered upon a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we said to him: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and do not narrate to us what you heard from people. They said: So they pressed him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us and said: I warn you of al-Masih al-Dajjal, I warn you of al-Masih al-Dajjal. He is a man with a wiped eye. Ibn Awn said: I think he said: the left. He stays in the earth forty mornings, with him are mountains of bread and rivers of water. His authority reaches every watering place. He does not come to four mosques. And he mentioned the Sacred Mosque and al-Aqsa Mosque and al-Tur and Medina. Except that whatever of that is, know that Allah is not one-eyed. Allah is not one-eyed. Allah is not one-eyed. Ibn Awn said: And I think in his hadith: He is given power over a man of mankind, so he kills him, then revives him, and is not given power over other than him."
"24084","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated to us Shubah, from Sulayman, from Mujahid, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, that he said: I came to a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said to him: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about al-Dajjal, and do not narrate to me from other than you, even if with you it is truthful. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I warned you of the trial of al-Dajjal. There is no prophet but he warned his people or his nation of him. He is dark, curly, one-eyed, his left eye. He rains but does not grow trees. He is given power over a soul, so he kills it, then revives it, and is not given power over other than it. With him are a garden and a fire, and a river and water, and a mountain of bread. His garden is a fire, and his fire is a garden. He stays among you forty mornings, coming to every watering place except four mosques: the Sacred Mosque, and the mosque of Medina, and al-Tur, and al-Aqsa Mosque. If it is confused for you or made similar, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is not one-eyed."
"24085","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, informed to us Sufyan, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Mujahid, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Azdi, he said: I went, I and a man of the Ansar, to a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we said: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned about al-Dajjal, and do not narrate to us from other than him, even if truthful. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: I warned you of al-Dajjal, three times. There was no prophet before me but he warned his nation of him. He is among you, O nation. He is curly, dark, with a wiped left eye. With him are a garden and a fire. So his fire is a garden, and his garden is a fire. And with him is a mountain of bread and a river of water. He rains rain but does not grow trees. He is given power over a soul, so he kills it, and is not given power over other than it. He stays in the earth forty mornings, reaching every watering place in it, and does not approach four mosques: the Sacred Mosque, and the mosque of Medina, and the mosque of al-Tur, and al-Aqsa Mosque. And whatever is made similar to you, your Lord is not one-eyed."
